program power_op

? `**` is right-associative power yielding float (C pow). It used to
? infer int, so print showed garbage (a double read as %d) whenever the
? value was not first stored into a variable (which truncated honestly).

@ main ||:
	expected: []
	expected.push|"8"|
	expected.push|"8"|
	expected.push|"512"|
	expected.push|"big"|

	print|2 ** 3|
	a: 2 ** 3
	print|a|
	print|2 ** 3 ** 2|
	if 2 ** 3 > 7 then
		print|"big"|
	$
	print|expected|
$
